\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }{\fs24 \tab The inventory screen consists of 3 parts. The top part represents what
 you are wearing and holding on your body. The bottom part shows what things you have in your backpack.. The bar on the bottom left shows the stats of the currently selected item. To put something on, select it in your backpack by using the }{\b\fs24 
arrow keys}{\fs24  and press }{\b\fs24 Enter}{\fs24 . To take something off, select the item on your body and press }{\b\fs24 Backspace}{\fs24 
. Unlike the Character and Spell Book screens, opening up your inventory during a fight takes a turn so it is generally a good idea to make sure you are wearing the right equipment before entering combat.
\par }\pard \ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 
In stores, the cost of the currently selected item and the money you have are shown at the bottom of the screen. To buy something, you must select the item and press }{\b\fs24 Enter}{\fs24  to purchase it. To sell an item, you must press }{\b\fs24 S}{
\fs24  to go to the sell screen and select the item you want to sell by pressing }{\b\fs24 Backspace}{\fs24 . The price the peddler will pay for the item you are selling is shown at the bottom. You can return to the buy screen by pressing }{\b\fs24 B}{
\fs24 . 
\par There are many types of weapons in the game. Selecting one in your inventory shows its stats. The underlined number preceded by }{\fs24 \lquote Str\rquote }{\fs24  (}{\fs24\ul Str 20) }{\fs24 shows the Strength requirement needed to use the weapon. The }{
\fs24 \lquote Atk\rquote }{\fs24  symbol states what the weapon adds to your overall chance of hitting the enemy. \lquote }{\fs24 P}{\b\fs24 =}{\fs24 \rquote }{\b\fs24  }{\fs24 states the average damage the weapon does. For example, a staff has }{
\fs24\ul Str 20}{\fs24 , Atk+28, and P=5. This means that to use the staff, you will need to have at least 20 Strength, the staff will add 28% to your chance of attack, and the staff will do an average of 
5 damage. Some weapons have special uses and have little icons on the lower-right corner to indicate them. Some (like the staff) have a 20% chance of blocking any melee attack and have a shield icon by them. Some (like the rapier) have a 20% chance of dou
b
le hitting an enemy when the first hit is made. They have an icon with 2 crossed lines by them. Some weapons (like the spear) are able to pierce the armor of monsters and thus do more damage to armored foes than normal weapons because their damage is not 
a
ffected by armor. They have a rectangle with a line going through it as an icon by them. Some weapons (like the sling) are long-ranged weapons that cannot be used in melee and have a bow icon by them. Some have to be wielded with 2 hands and their icons h
ave a 2 on them.}{\b\fs24 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\fs24 \tab }{\fs24 
Armor and helmets add wa and ma (wa-weapon armor,  ma-magic armor). They will give your character additional armor, which takes off some damage every time you are hit. Shields will add to your character\rquote s Defense value. Jewelry and magical
 items might add to any of the above categories.  
\par \tab Intelligence-boosting items can be used by having them equipped during a level up to allow you to memorize spells with Intelligence requirements that are higher than your Intelligence. For example, if you
r Intelligence is 14, you cannot learn the Flame spell which needs }{\fs24\ul Int 15}{\fs24 . However, if you put on a helmet that adds 1 to your Intelligence, you will be able to memorize this spell.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s6\ql \fi720\li2880\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel5\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {7   Spell Book
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {The spells that you have or are memorizing are displayed 
in 2 columns. You can cast them by selecting one and pressing }{\b Enter}{. If the spell needs a target, you can move the target cursor with the }{\b arrow keys}{ and select a square by pressing }{\b Enter}{. If you don\rquote 
t want to cast the spell, you can press }{\b Esc}{ instead of }{\b Enter}{ to not cast it. You can use one of the }{\b F1-F9}{ keys to preset a key for you to push so that you don\rquote t have to go to the spell book each time you cast. The }{\b F}{
 key you set will be displayed at the left of each spell icon. The blue number at the right of eac
h spell icon shows how much mana is needed to cast the spell. The white number is what Intelligence level is needed for you to cast the spell. If one of those numbers is red, you cannot cast a spell because you don\rquote 
t satisfy one of the conditions needed to
 cast it. After a level up, if your Intelligence is high enough and you are not learning any spells at the moment, you can choose to memorize (learn) a new spell. Spells that are being memorized cannot be used. They have a gray background and a yellow num
ber at top right to show how many level ups it will take for you to finish learning them. You can memorize only one spell at a time.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {A complete and }{\b very useful}{ list of spells\rquote 
 stats is in the Spells.xls file in the /thequest folder. The following are brief descriptions of the spells. Keep these in mind when you are deciding which spells to memorize.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }{\b\fs24 Heal}{\fs24 - heal yourself for a certain amount of hit points. A very important spell.
\par }{\b\fs24 
\par Flame- }{\fs24 ranged magical attack. The actual damage dealt by magical attacks can be +-33% of the spell\rquote s power. Thus, if a spell\rquote 
s power is 6, it may do 4-8 damage. In addition, monsters with magic resistance will take less damage (or sometimes no damage) from magical attacks
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Teleport}{\fs24 - instantly change your location. This is a good tactical spell and it can also move you to certain unreachable places.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Shield}{\fs24 - creates a shield around you that absorbs all (weapon, ranged, magical) attacks with power less that or equal to 10. If the attack\rquote s power is larger than 10, the        
\par shield does nothing. This spell is especially valuable since it will protect you from most ranged attacks.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Ring of Ice}{\fs24 - holds an enemy in one place for 10 turns or until it is attacked. The spell works on all enemies whose magic resistance is less than 10 (and that is almost all of them). The enemy can still attack you while it\rquote 
s feet are frozen. Combined with ranged weapons, this spell can be deadly.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Black Ward}{\fs24 - does damage to all enemies in the 8 squares around you.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Invisibility}{\fs24 - makes you invisible, disappears w
hen you cast, attack, or 30 turns have passed, the spell has a 50% of working but mana is not wasted if the spell fails. Some enemies will not be fooled by this spell and still see you. However, it can be a lifesaver (if it works) in deadly situations and
 is also good for sneaking up on vulnerable enemies.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Summon Skeleton}{\fs24 - summons a skeleton. The creature has low hp but can deal damage. It will attack the closest enemy and cannot be controlled. All summoned creatures disappear when you leave the area. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Inferno}{\fs24 - ranged magical attack.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Restore}{\fs24 - heal yourself for a certain amount of hit points. It is more mana-efficient than Heal.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Life Drain}{\fs24 - does damage to an enemy and adds to your life the amount of damage dealt.
\par This spell works best on enemies with a low magic resistance.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Thunder Bolt}{\fs24 - ranged magical attack.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Shield of Fire}{\fs24 - doesn\rquote t actually protect the caster, but instead deals damage to any nearby creatures every turn. The earlier you get this spell, the better since enemies with lower magic resistance will take more damage.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Deteriorate}{\fs24 - takes all of the caster\rquote s mana (no matter how much mana the caster has) and converts it into 100 damage that is dealt to a nearby enemy. A very powerful and efficient spell that should be used every time the caster is
 low on mana. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Summon Stone Knight}{\fs24 - this creature can take a very large amount of damage but does 
\par not attack well. It functions well as a protector, especially for vulnerable classes that can dish out ranged or spell damage while the summoned creature is being hit.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Earthquake}{\fs24 - this is a ranged area effect spell. It does a fair amount of damage to each 
\par }\pard\plain \s17\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
creature within the area, sometimes doubling or tripling the damage done to the monster in the center of the earthquake. It is best to obtain this spell a
s early as possible (if you think you are going to need it), since it does less damage to enemies with higher magic resistance.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 
\par }{\b\fs24 Cure }{\fs24 - heal yourself for a certain amount of hit points. It is more mana-efficient that Restore.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Summon Scorpion}{\fs24 - the scorpion does a great deal of damage but is physically weak. The scorpion can be very deadly if the caster can keep it from being killed.
\par }{\b\fs24 
\par Meteor}{\fs24  \endash  ranged magical attack
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Dark Hour - }{\fs24 takes all of the caster\rquote s mana and does damage 6 times to all the
\par creatures in the 8 squares near the caster.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s6\ql \li2880\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel5\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {8  Skills and Faults  
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s4\qc \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b Skills
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 Ambidexterity-  can hold 2 weapons (which allows you to make 2 attacks during melee, 
\par }\pard \ql \li1620\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1620\itap0 {\fs24 one for each weapon). Note: The secondary weapon\rquote s }{\fs24\ul Str}{\fs24  requirement must be less than or equal to }{\i\fs24 half }{\fs24 of your
 Strength. Thus, if your Strength is 50, you can hold one weapon with }{\fs24\ul Str 50 }{\fs24 and another with }{\fs24\ul Str 25.}{\fs24 
\par You can also hold 2 shields if you want to maximize your Defense. The secondary shield\rquote s }{\fs24\ul Str }{\fs24 requirement must be less than or equal to your Strength. Thus, if your Strength is 30, you can hold 2 shields with }{\fs24\ul Str 30}{
\fs24 .
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 Bargaining-        non-potion prices are cheaper by 30% when you buy at stores.
\par Marksmanship-  get a 30% Attack bonus when you use ranged weaponry.
\par Scholar-              Every other level up you will be able to choose where to assign a second 
\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\fs24     experience point instead of it being assigned randomly.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 Memorization-    takes 2 levels instead of 3 to learn spells.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\qc \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b Faults
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 Honor-                can\rquote t run away once started a fight (you must finish an enemy). 
\par Rashness-           spells will not work 20% of the time (Note: a fizzle will not cost you
\par }\pard \ql \fi240\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\fs24 any mana and after a fizzle your next attempt to cast will always be   
\par successful)    
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 Cowardice-         fight much worse when your Life is less than 30%  (your Attack is cut 
\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\fs24     in half)
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 \tab \tab \tab      
\par }\pard \ql \li2160\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0 {\fs24 Note: not all classes can have certain skills and faults.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\fs24 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\ql \li2880\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel6\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {   9 Fighting
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Let\rquote 
s say you are about to hit an enemy. Your Attack is 80, Defense is 20,  Power is 6,  and weapon armor is 2. Your enemy has Attack 90, Defense 20, Power 5, and has weapon armor 1. The enemy\rquote 
s Defense is subtracted from your Attack (80-20=60), and so you have a 60% chance to hit your enemy every time you attack. When you hit the monster, the damage you do will range from 4 to 8 (+-33% of your Power). The monster\rquote 
s weapon armor will be subtracted from the damage, and the resulting damage will be taken out of the monster\rquote s hit points. The monster has a 70% (90-20=70) to hit you when it attacks and will do 4 to 6 (+-33% of its power) damage, 
from which your weapon armor (2) will be subtracted. Thus, if the monster hits you for 6 damage, you will lose 4 hit points and the rest will be absorbed by your armor. 
\par Magical attacks never miss, but they can be absorbed with magical armor. If a monster 
casts a flame spell at you, your magic armor will be subtracted from the damage the spell does and the rest will be subtracted from your life. Thus, if a spell is about to do 9 damage to you and you have 6 magic armor, the spell will only damage you for 3
 
hit points. In case of ranged attacks, the closer one is to his target, the more accurate the attack. If you move closer to your enemy by one space, your Attack % increases by 10%. Also, ranged weapons, just like piercing weapons, are not affected by armo
r
. If you miss an enemy or its weapon armor completely absorbs your hit, a white shield will be displayed over the enemy. If you use magic on an enemy and its magic armor absorbs all of the damage, a yellow shield will be displayed over the enemy. If your 
life drops to 0 or below, you will begin to bleed. You must restore your hit points as soon as possible before your bleed to death. Some monsters also have a chance of poisoning you every time they successfully damage you.
\par }\pard\plain \s7\ql \li3600\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel6\adjustright\rin0\lin3600\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par 10 The Classes
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par \tab }{\fs24 There are four classes you can choose to play as in The Quest:  Knight, Mage, Monk, and Rogue. 
\par 
\par The Knight is inclined toward melee combat and has the most hit points. He focuses on his Strength and is ambidextrous. 
\par 
\par The Mage uses a wide variety of spells and has the most mana. He focuses on his Intelligence and has the memorization skill. 
\par 
\par The Monk is a mix between a Mage and a Knight, and will be able to fight as well as he can cast. He has the scholar skill which helps him balance his Intelligence and Strength. 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {The
 Rogue is the most proficient with ranged weapons since he focuses on his Accuracy and also has the marksmanship skill. The Rogue also maintains high Dexterity which allows him to be the best at hitting enemies with few misses and dodging enemy attacks.

\par }\pard \s15\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {
\par N
ote: no matter which class you chose, you will have to use different tactics at different points in the game. So even if you are a Mage, you might want to melee instead of casting spells when you are fighting enemies with high magic resistance. Also, ther
e is no \lquote easy class\rquote , so make sure you pick the one that\rquote s right for you.
\par }\pard\plain \s6\ql \fi720\li2880\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel5\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par 11  Level Up
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s16\ql \fi360\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Every time you move up a level, you will get points distributed to Strength, Intelligence, Accuracy, and Dexterity. 3 points are distributed randomly, and the categorie
s that were added to will be highlighted in purple. You will be able to assign the 4th point to the category of your choosing by pressing }{\b Enter}{
. An increase in Strength also adds an additional point to life, while increasing Intelligence also adds 1 point 
to mana. Furthermore, points will be added to your max mana and life every level up according to your class. A Knight gains 7 hp and 3 mana, a Mage gains 1 hp and 5 mana, a Rogue gains 4 hp and 4 mana, and a Monk gains 3 hp and 3 mana. If you have no spel
ls you are currently memorizing and are intelligent enough, you will be able to choose a spell to memorize. All spells take the same amount of levels to be memorized but the number depends on your memorization skill. 
\par It is possible to change classes. If yo
u are a Knight and allow your Intelligence to get almost as high as your Strength you will become a Monk. Also, if you are a Monk and your Intelligence becomes much larger than your Strength, you will become a Mage. In other words, the way in which you ma
n
age your attributes will affect your class. A Knight must keep his Strength at least 4 points above his Intelligence. A Mage must keep his Intelligence at least 4 points above his Strength. A Monk must keep his Intelligence and Strength within 3 points of
 each other. Finally, a Rogue must keep his combined Accuracy and Dexterity larger than his combined Intelligence and Strength.
\par When changing your class, you will acquire the skill of your new class, but lose the skill of your old one. The way in which you 
gain hp and mana per level up will also change. It might or might not be beneficial to change classes. If you are a Rogue and you depend on your marksmanship skill, you should be careful not to put too many points into Strength and Intelligence or you wil
l change classes and lose your skill. On the other hand, if you are a Rogue and you almost never use ranged weapons, it will be to your advantage to change classes and gain a skill that will be more useful to you.
\par 
\par }\pard \s16\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b 12   Startup Guide
\par }\pard \s16\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b 
\par }{\tab At the title screen, select \lquote new game\rquote 
. After the introduction, you will be able to select your class. If you are unsure as to which class to pick, you can answer questions and your class will be picked for you according to your answers. Then, you will see a list of skills wit
h one skill having  a \lquote +\rquote 
 next to it. That skill comes with your class. You will be able to select an additional skill as well as one fault. According to your class, some skills and faults will be blacked out and you will be unable to select them. There is
 no right or wrong combination of class+skills+fault. However, the choice you make will have a BIG effect on how you will play the game. For example, if you are Rogue and chose the ambidexterity skill, expect to be doing some melee fighting with 2 weapons
 
as well as increasing your Strength as much as you can so that you can wield better weapons in both hands. Of course, you can always ignore a skill but it is not to your advantage to do so, and you need all the advantages you can get. When choosing a faul
t, keep in mind that your are choosing a real weakness. It is probably not wise to select \lquote rashness\rquote  as a fault if you intend to do a lot of casting. On the other hand, all classes use magic and so having \lquote rashness\rquote 
 as a fault will still affect you.  
\par }\pard \s16\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {When 
the game starts, you are alone and there are no monsters near. On the right side of the screen you will see a circle displaying your life and a triangle displaying your mana. Take the time to look at your inventory ( }{\b I}{
 ) and make sure that you have a weapon. Not all classes start with one and if you don\rquote t have one, it should be your first priority to find one. Also, take a look at the spell book ( }{\b S }{
) to see if you can cast any spells yet. Look at the  character screen ( }{\b C}{ ) which displays important information about your character. There is a red potion nearby. Walk toward it by using the }{\b arrow keys}{ and pick it up ( }{\b Enter}{ ). A 
\lquote 1\rquote  should appear next to the red potion in the potion display at the bottom of the screen. To use a potion you must press a number }{\b 1}{-}{\b 8}{
 for that particular potion if you have it. If you walk to the right edge of the screen and then move right again, you will enter a new area where you will see some enemies. If you have a weapon, you can attack one of them by walking into it. If you hit
 an enemy, you will see a sword animation over the enemy. If you miss, a shield will be shown over the monster. Remember that the combat is turn-based and you don\rquote 
t have to rush. Keep an eye on your life as you fight since every time you are hit, the red l
ife will drain away in the circle. Also, remember that it is always best to fight one enemy at a time if you can. If you are a Mage, you can cast a flame spell instead of using melee. However, it might be easier to kill these monsters with melee instead o
f using up mana. If you have a sling in your inventory, you can equip it and some pebbles and attack the monsters from afar by pressing }{\b Tab}{ to select the monster and then pressing }{\b Space}{ to shoot at it (you only have to press }{\b Tab}{
 once to select your target). After you destroy your first enemies, don\rquote t forget to save. After a few fights, your health might be low. If you have the Heal spell, you can heal yourself to restore your hit points. If you don\rquote 
t have the Heal spell, you will have to use one of your poti
ons. There is a village nearby where you can buy and sell items as well as talk to the people that live there. To talk to a person, simply walk into him the same way you walk into a monster to attack it. If you ever feel the need to kill a friendly person
, press }{\b K}{ to activate killer mode and walk into the person to attack him. This should be enough to get you started on your journey. Good luck\'85
\par }\pard \s16\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {
\par }\pard\plain \s7\ql \li2880\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel6\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {     13   Final Words of Advice
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {1. Check your inventory when you begin the game. Not all classes start with weapons.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 2. Try to fight 1 monster at a time (get in good a position).
\par 3. Running away is often a good strategy.
\par 4. Do not neglect ranged weaponry, you can kill a lot of monsters without getting   
\par     scratched using it.
\par 5. Each class plays a bit differently. Try different strategies. If you are running out of 
\par     money and potions, you are probably in need of new tactics.
\par 6. Don\rquote t neglect Dexterity. Who cares if you can wield a an awesome weapon   
\par     if you miss with it all the time. Who cares if you can cast powerful spells when        
\par     monsters get free hits at you because your Defense is too low. 
\par 7. Try to pick your fights in the beginning (going into that place with 12 imps when you 
\par      are Level 1 is not wise).
\par 8. Upgrade your equipment (wielding a staff will be much more beneficial than holding a 
\par      club).
\par 9. There is only 1 save slot, use it wisely. This means DON\rquote T SAVE IN A PLACE YOU CAN\rquote T GET OUT OF!
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {10. Some weapons allow you to do special things (Ex: Staff- block attacks),  there is an   
\par       icon indicating the effect. Make sure you are aware of these important characteristics.
\par 11. Don\rquote t attack the scorpions unless you have some poison potions at hand.                                    
\par 12. Save early and save often.
\par 13}{\b . }{\i Always}{ stock up on potions before going to the next map, they will cost more there.\line 14. Going to the Spell Book or Character Screen does not use up your turn. Going to the    
\par       Inventory does.
\par 15. Setting the F1-F9 keys to cast spells makes casting easier and faster.
\par 16. It is impossible for enemies with ranged attacks to hit you when your are right next to 
\par       them (1 space away), but when you are 2 spaces away it is the easiest.
\par 17. If one weapon costs more than another, it does not mean that that weapon is the better     
\par       of the two. It is up to you to make the decision.
\par 18. Just because you are a Mage doesn\rquote t mean that you have to put every level up point   
\par       into Intelligence. Though you should concentrate on your most important    
\par       attributes, don\rquote t neglect others. Being a pure fighter or a pure caster is certainly 
\par       possible but being balanced has many advantages.
\par 19. The types of potions you purchase matter greatly. If you have 20 max hp, 30 max 
\par        mana, and can cast heal, it is much more efficient to buy blue potions since for the   
\par        price of one you can give yourself 90 hp (cast heal 3 times), but if you buy a red 
\par        potion for the same  price, all you get is 20 hp (a 70 hp difference!). The type of 
\par        potion that is best for you will vary at times according to your class. It is up to you to 
\par       decide which you should be buying.
\par 20. Try different strategies. Even if you are a great melee fighter, it is wiser to use ranged 
\par        weapons on some enemies. If you are a Mage and are fighting monsters with high 
\par        magic resistance, it might make sense to use melee or ranged weapons instead of 
\par        spells.
\par 21.  Make sure that you always have a Cyan potion at hand. You never know when you 
\par        will need it.
\par 22.  It is possible to try to steal items from certain npcs. You can attack them, run away, 
\par        and then take what they were holding (you will see it if the npc has something of    
\par        value) before they started chasing you. Of course, you can always kill the npc, but      
\par        your reputation\'85
\par 23.  It is not always possible to obtain the keys to all doors. Sometimes, you will have to 
\par        find others ways of getting to places.
\par 24.  This may sound obvious but\'85talk to the npcs and pay attention to all of the 
\par         information you get. 
\par 25.   Good Luck!
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 
\par }\pard\plain \s5\ql \li2160\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel4\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0 \b\fs28\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {14   Combat Formulas }{\b0 (in case you are interested)
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Attack(%)=hero dex+35+weapon+special effects.
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Defense(%)=hero dex+10+shield+special effects.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 Ranged Attack(%)=hero acc*2+15+(8-distance)*10+special effects. If distance=1, ranged weapons can\rquote 
t be used.
\par }\pard \ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 
The chances of all non-magic attacks are equal to the Attack % of the attacker minus the Defense % of the defender. Magic attacks never miss but can still be absorbed by magic armor.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {                                                 }{\b\fs28 15 Troubleshooting
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 
\par Q.   When you try to play the game, you see only a black screen with a flashing white line at the top. 
\par A.   To fix the problem, you must first right-click on the \lquote The Quest.exe\rquote  program file in the Windows Explorer and select \lquote Properties\rquote . There, you must click on the \lquote Screen\rquote  tab. Where it says \lquote Usage
\rquote , you must make sure that \lquote Full-screen\rquote  is selected and }{\b\fs24 not}{\fs24  \lquote Window\rquote . Click \lquote Ok\rquote  to finish. Now, try to run the game.
\par }\pard \ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 
\par If that doesn\rquote t solve your problem and the game still refuses to run without giving you an error message, try running it directly from DOS (assuming your operating system supports DOS). 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Q.  You get the following error--  \'93Graphics Error: Device BGI driver file not found
\'85\'94
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs24 A.  The Rpg.exe file is either not in the \\thequest directory or the /bgi folder is not in the     

\par        /thequest directory.
\par 
\par Q.  You get the following error--  \'93Error: file not found\'94 or \'93Error: items.dat file not 
\par        found in the data folder.\'94
\par A.   Make sure that all the files in the data folder stay there. Do not move them or alter 
\par        them in any way.
\par 
\par Q.  The game runs slowly. The loading screens take a long time. Going from room to 
\par        room takes a long time.
\par A.  The speed of the game depends on the speed of the processor of your computer. The 
\par       higher the speed, the better the performance. However, the game will still run on    
\par       machines as slow as 366/33s as long as it\rquote s an IBM.
\par 
\par Q.  You get the following error -- \'93Error: you have too many save files, you must delete 
\par        at least one to play.\'94
\par A.  You will see this message if you have created 20 characters and are trying to create 
\par        another one. To fix the problem, you must delete save file #20 (save20.dat) in the  
\par       /data folder (in Windows Explorer) to create room for your new one.
\par 
\par Q.  Somehow I managed to erase an important file and now the game will not work. 
\par       What do I do now?
\par A.  You can re-download the zip file from wherever you got it or e-mail me at 
